"""
bt-dualboot-sync - stop re-pairing Bluetooth devices on Windows/Linux dual-boot PCs.

Why you have to re-pair: when a device pairs, the PC and the device agree on a
secret "link key". Windows and Linux each store their own copy, so pairing in
one OS replaces the key on the device and the other OS's copy becomes invalid.

This tool makes both OSes use the SAME key:
  * Windows -> Linux: reads the Windows SYSTEM registry hive directly from the
    Windows partition (read-only, no extra packages) and writes the keys into
    BlueZ (/var/lib/bluetooth).
  * Linux -> Windows: exports BlueZ keys to the EFI partition, where the
    companion Windows script (windows/bt-dualboot-sync.ps1) imports them.

Zero dependencies: Python 3.7+ standard library only.
"""
